Clinical Course: Symptoms are episodic and typically self-limiting, often related to dietary intake and gut motility changes.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Seek immediate medical attention if your stomach becomes hard and rigid, if you develop a high fever, or if you stop passing gas completely.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Excess gas in the digestive tract is usually caused by the fermentation of undigested foods by gut bacteria. Identifying these foods helps reduce gas production.
Actionable Steps: Eat slowly, chew food thoroughly, and avoid carbonated beverages. Take simethicone as needed for trapped gas.

